WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.821 --> 00:00:06.940
This page shows the rhythm of the whole term at once, so no week ever surprises you.

2
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:17.887
Read the rhythm first. Most weeks meet live. The delivery label on every week page names that week's mode, so you always know how a week works before you plan it.

3
00:00:17.887 --> 00:00:28.922
Note the asynchronous weeks and their purpose. Week 4 applies the early foundations independently, Week 11 is a synthesis point before the final live stretch, and Weeks 13 and 14 protect focused completion and closure.

4
00:00:28.922 --> 00:00:39.988
Follow the five moves each week. Prepare, meet or work independently, return for the activity and reflection, save your notes, and carry the strongest work forward.

5
00:00:39.988 --> 00:00:50.842
Build the cartography as you go. Your weekly notes and journal entries feed the Personal Cartography sequence. Building it slowly beats inventing it at the end.

6
00:00:50.842 --> 00:00:59.188
Start with the current week. The button at the bottom opens the weekly journey. Blackboard holds all graded submissions.

7
00:00:59.188 --> 00:01:01.793
Nothing here is graded.

8
00:01:01.793 --> 00:01:07.601
Where next: Open Calendar and Due Dates to put exact dates against this rhythm.
